## Optional Madi continuity

- Use Madi only when this project and a machine-local workstream binding have been explicitly configured.
- The `PreCompact` hook only observes the lifecycle boundary. It does not save a revision by itself and must never open or summarize a transcript.
- Before compaction or an agent switch, select and sanitize semantic continuity yourself. Do not include raw conversation text, tool output, native paths, model data, or agent identity.
- Submit only that host-composed checkpoint through the explicit Madi checkpoint command. A receiving agent uses a distinct session linked with `continues_from`; select its head only with an explicit Core command.
- If translation, checkpointing, or Madi itself fails, continue ordinary Codex work and retry a manual checkpoint later.

